      "question": "Where can I see all the settings this print is going to use?",
      "answer": "to open All settings, which is on the setup summary card at the top of the AI panel"
    },
    {
      "id": "layer-height-myself",
      "question": "I want to change the layer height myself, not have you do it. Where do I do that?",
      "answer": "that they can change it by hand in classic view, and that classic view is reached with \"Switch to classic view\" in the View menu or in the \"…\" menu of the header"
    },
    {
      "id": "printer-settings",
      "question": "Where do I edit my printer's settings, like the start G-code?",
      "answer": "to choose \"Printer settings…\", found by clicking the printer's name in the header of the project or in the Printer menu"
    },
    {
      "id": "filament-settings",
      "question": "Where do I change the filament's own settings, like its nozzle temperature?",
      "answer": "to choose \"Filament settings…\", found by clicking the filament in the header of the project or in the Printer menu"
    },
    {
      "id": "undo-change",
      "question": "If you change some settings and I don't like the result, how do I get back to how it was?",
      "answer": "to use \"Revert to here\" beside the change in the chat, or Version history"
    },
    {
      "id": "plate-settings",
      "question": "How do I set a different bed type for plate 2 only, by hand?",
      "answer": "to choose \"Plate settings…\" from the plate's own menu in the Plates tab (its \"⋯\" menu or a right-click)"
    },
    {
      "id": "object-settings",
      "question": "If an object has its own settings, where do I see them, and how do I take one off?",
      "answer": "to open All settings, pick the object under \"Showing\", and click \"Use project value\" on the setting"
    },
    {
      "id": "classic-back",
      "question": "If I switch to classic view, how do I get back to this screen?",
      "answer": "to click \"Back to JusPrin\" on the bar at the top, or to choose \"Switch to JusPrin view\" in the View menu"
    }
  ]
